  "boundary": {
    "id": "mCoreRewindRestore-currentState-map-failure",
    "production_caller": "src/core/rewind.c:mCoreRewindRestore",
    "source_lines": ["src/core/rewind.c:123-170", "src/core/rewind.c:144-162"],
    "contract": "The caller maps currentState and previousState, passes both results to the patch callback without checking either pointer or the callback result, calls unmap on both, swaps state VFiles, calls mCoreLoadStateNamed, ignores its result, and returns true after consuming the rewind entry.",
    "fault_injection": "The harness first initializes real pinned VFileMemChunk state, then replaces only the currentState map callback with a bounded test adapter that returns NULL once. The actual pinned mCoreRewindRestore implementation is compiled unchanged and executed.",
    "test_doubles": [
      "The map-failure adapter injects one NULL map result.",
      "The patch callback observes nullable inputs and returns false rather than dereferencing a NULL pointer.",
      "mCoreLoadStateNamed is stubbed to record the call and return false."
    ],
    "finding": "On the tested Linux host, the actual pinned caller still invokes the patch callback, unmaps both states including the failed mapping, swaps the state handles, calls the core-load stub, consumes one rewind entry, and returns true despite the NULL map and false patch/load results. The recovery control uses a fresh valid context; no in-place retry or production core callback is claimed."
  },
